# Documentation Rules (`docs/`)

Before creating, editing, or moving any `.md` file in this repository:

1. Read `docs/README.md` and check the matching `docs/01-`..`09-` subfolder first to avoid duplicates.
2. Follow `.agents/skills/docs-authoring/SKILL.md`:
   - Never place new `.md` files at repo root or directly under `docs/` (only `docs/README.md`).
   - Use the matching numbered topic folder (`docs/01-`..`09-`); new top-level folders must follow `NN-kebab-case`.
   - No spaces in filenames; relative links only; never embed local paths (`C:/...`, `D:/...`, `file:///...`).
   - Update `docs/README.md` if adding a key document or new topic folder.
3. Verify with `node scripts/check-docs-rule.mjs --ci`.
